<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="52385" href="schedule/2010/spring/PSYC/199/52385.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2010" href="schedule/2010.xml">2010</calendarYear><term id="120101" href="schedule/2010/spring.xml">Spring 2010</term><subject id="PSYC" href="schedule/2010/spring/PSYC.xml">Psychology</subject><course id="199" href="schedule/2010/spring/PSYC/199.xml">Undergraduate Open Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>GEN</sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course will begin with a reading and discussion of the "5 Psychological experiments that prove humanity is doomed."  We will critically evaluate these five studies and discuss the common threads that run within them.  We will then move into a study of positive psychology and a search for 5 psychological experiments that prove that humanity will survive.  This course is designed as a discussion course.  Group work and writing will be emphasized.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2010-01-19Z</startDate><endDate>2010-05-05Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:15 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>29</roomNumber><buildingName>Psychology Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Lucas" firstName="S">Lucas, S</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>